  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Resisting state capture from the grassroots: Civil society and public perceptions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to deepen understanding of state capture by focusing on the previously
overlooked role of public opinion in mitigating state capture and democratic backsliding. This study will investigate public attitudes towards state capture and evaluate the impact of communication campaigns that aim to foster civic engagement and to mobilise citizens, for example, to support anti-state capture interventions and vote for anti-state capture candidates in elections. The research will also explore potential risks of communications campaigns in this area, such as unintentionally reinforcing feelings of resignation or fostering populist sentiment and propose strategies to mitigate these challenges.</narrative>
  </description>
